NAME
       fsck.vfat - check and repair a FAT (vfat) file system

SYNOPSIS
       fsck.vfat [-n] [-y] DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       fsck.vfat (also called fsck.fat and dosfsck, from the dosfstools
       package) checks a FAT12, FAT16 or FAT32 file system, such as a USB
       stick or the EFI system partition, and repairs it. Unmount the file
       system first.

OPTIONS
       -n     Check only; change nothing.

       -y     Answer yes to every question.

EXAMPLES
           umount /mnt/usb
           fsck.vfat -n /dev/vdb2

SEE ALSO
       fsck(8), mkfs.fat(8), fatlabel(8)
